The following method performs a binary search on a sorted array. The call <code>binarySearch(arr, 23)</code> is made, where <code>arr</code> is <code>{2, 5, 8, 12, 16, 23, 38, 56, 72, 91}</code>. Which sequence of values is assigned to <code>mid</code>?<pre class="formula-code"><code>public static int binarySearch(int[] arr, int target)
{
    int low = 0;
    int high = arr.length - 1;
    while (low &lt;= high)
    {
        int mid = (low + high) / 2;
        if (arr[mid] == target)
        {
            return mid;
        }
        else if (arr[mid] &lt; target)
        {
            low = mid + 1;
        }
        else
        {
            high = mid - 1;
        }
    }
    return -1;
}</code></pre>

